      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Potassium supplements can be a real concern with lisinopril, but you should **not** stop or start them without checking with your pharmacist or doctor first. That's because lisinopril can raise your potassium levels, and taking extra potassium could push them into a dangerous range. Leg cramps are a common side effect of lisinopril, but your doctor may need to adjust your dose or switch medications instead. Please call your prescriber's office today to discuss your symptoms and get a blood test to check your potassium levels before adding any supplement.",
